# The ROMs the Game Boy Pokémon companion's ROM tests expect (kiwami/GB-POKEMON.md, "The ROMs for the tests"), checked
# in the player's own folders by kiwami/tests/gbpk-roms.sh. None of them is in the repository. One line a file:
#   <sha1> <system> <required|optional> <game> <No-Intro file name>
# system is the folder the file is looked for in: gb in GB_ROMS (~/gb-companion/roms), gba in GBA_ROMS
# (~/gba-companion/roms), nds in NDS_ROMS (~/nds-companion/roms). A file is found by its SHA-1, whatever its name. The
# SHA-1s are PokeDaisy's (GameTitles.kt at 135ac809): pret's roms.sha1 for pokered, pokeyellow, pokegold, pokecrystal,
# pokeruby, pokefirered, pokeemerald, pokeplatinum and pokeheartgold, No-Intro's for Black, White, Black 2 and White 2.
# The gb lines' games are the data files' keys, and their SHA-1s those files' releases (gbpk-units checks both ways).

# Game Boy and Game Boy Color: what the companion's ROM tests read
ea9bcae617fdf159b045185467ae58b2e4a48b9a gb required red Pokemon - Red Version (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced).gb
d7037c83e1ae5b39bde3c30787637ba1d4c48ce2 gb required blue Pokemon - Blue Version (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced).gb
cc7d03262ebfaf2f06772c1a480c7d9d5f4a38e1 gb required yellow Pokemon - Yellow Version - Special Pikachu Edition (USA, Europe) (CGB+SGB Enhanced).gb
d8b8a3600a465308c9953dfa04f0081c05bdcb94 gb required gold Pokemon - Gold Version (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).gbc
49b163f7e57702bc939d642a18f591de55d92dae gb required silver Pokemon - Silver Version (USA, Europe) (SGB Enhanced) (GB Compatible).gbc
f2f52230b536214ef7c9924f483392993e226cfb gb required crystal Pokemon - Crystal Version (USA, Europe) (Rev 1).gbc
f4cd194bdee0d04ca4eac29e09b8e4e9d818c133 gb optional crystal Pokemon - Crystal Version (USA).gbc
a0fc810f1d4e124434f7be2c989ab5b5892ddf36 gb optional crystal Pokemon - Crystal Version (Australia).gbc

